    {
      "id": "diode-iv-r2-q1",
      "round": 2,
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "A short-base diode (\\(L\\gg W\\)) has area \\(100\\ \\mu\\mathrm{m^2}\\). N side: \\(N_D=10^{17}\\ \\mathrm{cm^{-3}}\\), \\(W_n=1\\ \\mu\\mathrm{m}\\), \\(D_p=10\\ \\mathrm{cm^2/s}\\). P side: \\(N_A=10^{18}\\ \\mathrm{cm^{-3}}\\), \\(W_p=1\\ \\mu\\mathrm{m}\\), \\(D_n=30\\ \\mathrm{cm^2/s}\\). \\(n_i=10^{10}\\ \\mathrm{cm^{-3}}\\). Using \\(I_S=qAn_i^2\\left(\\dfrac{D_p}{N_DW_n}+\\dfrac{D_n}{N_AW_p}\\right)\\), what is \\(I_S\\) in aA (\\(1\\ \\mathrm{aA}=10^{-18}\\ \\mathrm{A}\\))?",
